      "text": "That’s an intriguing question. In theory, if an AI system could learn, adapt, and generate new ideas without human input or guidance, it might develop a form of creativity that’s unique to its own architecture. However, whether that constitutes “true” creativity is still up for debate, since it would lack human experiences and emotions that often inspire human creativity.",
